      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_da404ad5",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: look_dude_a_second_hand_store; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two Black men in a poor, rural setting, with one man looking upward in apparent awe or excitement while the other looks on. The overlaid text reads 'look dude a second hand store !!'. The meme's intent is to portray Black people as being so impoverished or desperate that they are thrilled by the prospect of a second-hand store, implying a stereotype of laziness, lack of ambition, or contentment with minimal resources. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that reduces a group to a caricature of economic desperation and reinforces negative racial tropes. The juxtaposition of the image with the text is used to mock and demean Black individuals by associating them with poverty and a lack of aspiration, which is a form of racialized hate speech.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_33df63b8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
