    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c3cf9939",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The man expressing awe is mapped as the person who is excited about a second-hand store",
      "description": "The text 'look dude a second hand store !!' explicitly directs the viewer's attention to the man on the left, who is visually depicted in a state of awe. His body language (head tilted back, hand on neck) is mapped onto the textual description of being thrilled by a second-hand store, creating an analogical mapping where his reaction is interpreted as a response to the store. This mapping reinforces the stereotype that Black people are so impoverished they are ecstatic about minimal resources.",
